        "heading": "Verifying the new record before cutover",
        "paragraphs": [
          "Verification for onboarding task cleanup means checking that the onboarding task cleanup log links the source, the decision, and the approved close. A sent reminder or a closed ticket proves activity, not outcome. CustomerSuccessManagers reviews a small sample against the same definition each month. The sample should include one difficult case, not only the easy queue. The next owner should be able to see which fields were checked and which were left open.",
          "The review ends with one decision about onboarding task cleanup. Fix the source, simplify the field, change the queue, or stop the work until the owner decides. CustomerSuccessManagers gives each change an owner and a check date. That is how a onboarding task cleanup control improves instead of becoming another status meeting. Keep the note short enough to read during a live account review and specific enough to be tested later."
        ]
